 <p class="text-lg text-slate-700 italic">In April 2026, a first-time importer paid $4,200 in unnecessary duty on a single container of power banks — because their factory used the wrong 6-digit HS code on the commercial invoice. The mistake took 15 seconds to make and 3 months to fix. The 2026 US tariff stack creates more opportunities for this kind of error than any year in the last decade: Section 301 at 25%, a tiered Section 301 forced-labor tariff (10-12.5%) that replaced the expired Section 122 surcharge on July 24, 2026, and an IEEPA refund window most importers still don't know exists. This is not a reference guide — it's a mistake-prevention checklist for OEM buyers who can't afford to learn the hard way.</p>
